From 0002f69fbb577e969ab037a7d354e4dfcbe6ab16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:37:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Make quoted-subscript classification incremental per
 simple command

Review 5906053691 (t_d2a1c07ed00e87ab): one simple command with N quoted
subscript-like words re-tokenized its whole prefix per word, O(N x len).
QuotedNameClassifier now resumes tokenization at the previously classified
word and reuses a word's verdict for its later brackets, so each source
character is tokenized O(1) times; command position resolves from at most
64 leading words (fail closed beyond). Quoted compound-array elements,
a=("x[...]"), are values, not subscripts. The real-Bash prior-expansion
cross product is split into 4 wrapper shards under the per-file time cap.
